  "reading": "Static vacuum solutions of box sigma = 0 on Schwarzschild are A + B ln(1 - r_s/r) exactly. Regular at the horizon => B = 0 => sigma = const (no scalar hair). B != 0 diverges logarithmically at r_s. For a star R/r_s >> 1 and the horizon is never reached. The values xi, xi/2, 1/2 at r = r_s come only from evaluating the weak-field 1/r formula outside its domain; the inventory's xi/2 is enforced by the compactness clamp at 0.5 (sigma.py:301-302), not derived. 'sigma = xi/2 at any horizon' has no derivation from box sigma = -xi R.",
